=======================

This merged work is licensed AGPL-3.0 overall (see LICENSE).
It combines code and ideas from three open-source projects:

1. OpenShorts — https://github.com/mutonby/openshorts — MIT License
   (full text: licenses-MIT-openshorts.txt)
   What was taken: clip_selection.py vendored verbatim
   (merged_clipper/vendor/clip_selection.py); the pipeline shape
   (faster-whisper word timestamps, Gemini-or-local-LLM moment
   picking, smart 9:16 layouts, MCP/API concepts).

2. opensource-clipping — https://github.com/NaufalRizqullah/opensource-clipping — MIT License
   (full text: licenses-MIT-opensource-clipping.txt)
   What was taken: the pipeline shape (Faster-Whisper large-v3,
   Gemini curation, MediaPipe face tracking, karaoke subtitles,
   3-second cinematic hook teaser, auto-thumbnail, B-roll and
   uploader concepts). Its studio modules could not be imported
   directly (they require cv2 + mediapipe at import time), so the
   karaoke/hook/thumbnail features were reimplemented in lightweight
   ffmpeg/Pillow glue code — see README "What is new / reimplemented".

3. SupoClip — https://github.com/FujiwaraChoki/supoclip — AGPL-3.0
   What was taken (verbatim, in merged_clipper/vendor/):
     - supoclip_clip_duration.py (clip-length presets)
     - supoclip_caption_templates.py (caption templates)
     - supoclip_emoji_captions.py (emoji + emphasis annotation)
   What was taken as reimplemented features: the virality breakdown
   (hook / engagement / value / shareability, 0-25 each, total 0-100),
   Twitch/Kick import (via yt-dlp), provider handling
   (TRANSCRIPTION_PROVIDER / LLM env vars), the opening review idea,
   built-in editor concepts (clip.py edit), direct-publishing
   concepts (publish metadata + dry-run checklist) and the
   performance log (track.csv).
   NOT taken: the full Docker stack (Next.js + FastAPI + Postgres +
   Redis, 11 services) — far too heavy for a lightweight CLI.

